      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "684c5f82-c245-53dc-ad84-08fd0f28c139",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Battle of Okinawa, Operation Nordwind, World War II, Battle of Guadalcanal, Banana Wars\n- People: Pedro del Valle\n- Places: Okinawa, Alsace, Lorraine, northeastern France, Haiti, Nicaragua\n- Roles: Commanding General of the 1st Marine Division\n\nFacts:\n- Pedro del Valle served in World War I.\n- Pedro del Valle served in Haiti and Nicaragua during the Banana Wars of the 1920s.\n- Operation Nordwind was the last major German offensive of World War II on the Western Front.\n- Operation Nordwind began on 31 December 1944 in Alsace and Lorraine in northeastern France.\n- The Battle of Okinawa lasted 82 days from 1 April 1945 until 22 June 1945.\n- Operation Nordwind ended on 25 January 1945.\n- Pedro del Valle served in World War II at the Battle of Guadalcanal and at the Battle of Okinawa.\n- Pedro del Valle was the Commanding General of the 1st Marine Division at the Battle of Okinawa.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "f788dbbd-8b88-5700-ba09-beadb0b4522e",
        "text": "Page: Battle of Okinawa. Sentence: The 82-day battle lasted from April 1 until June 22, 1945.\nPage: Operation Nordwind. Sentence: Operation North Wind (German: \"Unternehmen Nordwind\" ) was the last major German offensive of World War II on the Western Front.\nPage: Operation Nordwind. Sentence: It began on 31 December 1944 in Alsace and Lorraine in northeastern France, and ended on 25 January.\nPage: Pedro del Valle. Sentence: His military career included service in World War I, Haiti and Nicaragua during the Banana Wars of the 1920s, and in World War II, the Battle of Guadalcanal and Battle of Okinawa (Commanding General of the 1st Marine Division).",
